        "id": "p16-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Construct a stem-and-leaf plot.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$$\\begin{array}{r|l}\\text{Stem}&\\text{Leaves}\\\\\\hline9&6\\;8\\;8\\;9\\;9\\;9\\;9\\\\10&0\\;0\\;1\\;1\\;2\\;2\\;3\\;4\\;5\\;8\\;8\\;9\\\\11&2\\;2\\;3\\;3\\;5\\;6\\;9\\\\12&1\\;2\\\\13&2\\;8\\;9\\\\14&2\\;3\\;4\\;5\\;7\\\\15&2\\;5\\;6\\\\16&7\\;7\\\\17&1\\end{array}$$\nKey: $10\\mid1$ represents $101\\text{ cm}$.",
          "worked": "Use the tens and hundreds digits as the stem and the units digit as the leaf. Arrange the leaves in increasing order within each stem.\n$$\\begin{array}{r|l}\\text{Stem}&\\text{Leaves}\\\\\\hline9&6\\;8\\;8\\;9\\;9\\;9\\;9\\\\10&0\\;0\\;1\\;1\\;2\\;2\\;3\\;4\\;5\\;8\\;8\\;9\\\\11&2\\;2\\;3\\;3\\;5\\;6\\;9\\\\12&1\\;2\\\\13&2\\;8\\;9\\\\14&2\\;3\\;4\\;5\\;7\\\\15&2\\;5\\;6\\\\16&7\\;7\\\\17&1\\end{array}$$\nKey: $10\\mid1$ represents $101\\text{ cm}$. There are 42 leaves, one for each student.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 75
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the median.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$112.5\\text{ cm}$",
          "worked": "There are 42 heights, so the middle values are the 21st and 22nd ordered heights: $112\\text{ cm}$ and $113\\text{ cm}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Median}&=\\frac{112+113}{2}\\\\\\text{Median}&=112.5\\text{ cm}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find the range.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$75\\text{ cm}$",
          "worked": "The lowest height is $96\\text{ cm}$ and the highest is $171\\text{ cm}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Range}&=171-96\\\\\\text{Range}&=75\\text{ cm}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
